# System architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  subgraph Sources
    PDS[Planetary Data System]
    E[Earth elevation/observation]
    G[Governance/site records]
  end
  subgraph Core[Planetary Analog OS core]
    SL[Source lock]
    MO[Mission ontology]
    DP[Data processing]
    FE[Feature engine]
    CG[Comparison + gap engine]
    PG[Protocol generator]
    EG[Evidence graph]
  end
  subgraph Surfaces
    WB[Study workbench]
    DOC[Docs/evaluation]
    PKG[Portable study package]
    API[Institutional API future]
  end
  PDS --> SL
  E --> SL
  G --> SL
  SL --> DP
  MO --> CG
  DP --> FE --> CG
  CG --> PG
  SL --> EG
  MO --> EG
  FE --> EG
  CG --> EG
  PG --> EG
  EG --> WB
  EG --> DOC
  EG --> PKG
  EG --> API
```

## Visual design intent

- Source textures should feel like mineral/terrain evidence, not generic SaaS.
- The high-impact visual is the connected evidence trace.
- Every visual layer is paired with an accessible table/claim.
- The product remains calm when evidence is weak: uncertainty is visual hierarchy, not a footnote.
